🚀 How to use
1. Download the PowerShell script

Download Test-M365Endpoints.ps1 and save it in a folder named:

C:\Scripts

2. Open PowerShell

Open a PowerShell window and run the following command to allow the script to run for the current PowerShell session:

Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass


This setting applies only to the current PowerShell process.

3. Navigate to the Scripts folder

Run:

cd C:\Scripts

4. Run the script

Execute the script with:

.\Test-M365Endpoints.ps1


The script will then run the Microsoft 365 endpoint connectivity tests and display the results.

💡 Full command sequence
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass
cd C:\Scripts
.\Test-M365Endpoints.ps1

📊 Test results

The network testing script generates two CSV reports in %USERPROFILE% in M365-NetworkTests folder :

M365_NetworkTests_20261022_233303.csv: contains the results of all network connectivity tests performed against the Microsoft 365 endpoints.
M365_NetworkFailures_20261022_233303.csv: provides a dedicated report containing the connectivity tests that failed, making it easier to quickly identify endpoints that may be blocked or unreachable.

This approach provides both a complete view of the network tests and a focused view of detected connectivity issues, making troubleshooting faster and easier.
